@startuml activity-navigation
' Chapter 3, Software design, section 3.3: navigation between activities.
' Renders with any PlantUML processor, for example
' https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml or a local toolchain:
' plantuml docs/diagrams/activity-navigation.puml
' Source of the facts shown here: app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml, the five
' activity classes under app/src/main/java/de/miangohar/overload/ui, and
' docs/decision-log.md ADR-0002.

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #B8A000
}

title Overload, navigation between the five activities

state "DashboardActivity\n<b>launcher</b>, exported" as Dashboard
state "GoalActivity" as Goal
state "LogEntryActivity" as LogEntry
state "HistoryActivity" as History
state "WeekDetailActivity" as WeekDetail
state "system notification\n(outside the five activities)" as Notification

Dashboard -[#000000]-> Goal : explicit Intent
Dashboard -[#000000]-> LogEntry : explicit Intent
Dashboard -[#000000]-> History : explicit Intent
History -[#000000]-> WeekDetail : explicit Intent\n+ EXTRA_WEEK_START_EPOCH_DAY
Notification -[#000000]-> LogEntry : explicit Intent (PendingIntent,\nFLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK)

Goal -[#888888,dashed]-> Dashboard : up, parentActivityName
LogEntry -[#888888,dashed]-> Dashboard : up, parentActivityName
History -[#888888,dashed]-> Dashboard : up, parentActivityName
WeekDetail -[#888888,dashed]-> History : up, parentActivityName

note right of Dashboard
  Every non launcher activity declares
  android:exported="false"; the manifest
  is the only place a target activity is
  named, never inferred from a route table.
end note

note bottom of WeekDetail
  The extra carries only the week's start
  date, not the caller's list state, so the
  two activities stay loosely coupled.
end note

note left of Dashboard
  One activity per screen, explicit intents
  rather than a single activity with a
  navigation graph, ADR-0002. This runs
  against current Android practice; accepted
  because the examination task names several
  activities as a requirement, which a nav
  graph inside one activity does not satisfy.
end note

@enduml
